  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ganipisetty China Rangaiah vs The State Of Ap on 16 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.6120 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 to A5 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.105 of 2019 of Bellamkonda Police Station, Guntur District, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 420, 120b of IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 15.09.2019 at 04.00 p.m., when the complainant along with his staff conducting vehicle search at Agriculture Market Check Post, Bellamkonda Cross Road, Bellamkonda Village and Mandal, intercepted the Ashok Layland Mini Tralee bearing No.AP 39TB 1538 and found the banned tobacco products in the said vehicle and on enquiry, the petitioners/A1 to A5 confessed that they are doing the business and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.105 of 2019 of Bellamkonda Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
